@page "/model"
@model ModelModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The Model · The Corner FC";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How good The Corner FC's match model is, in the open: its locked pre-kickoff record, how it compares with the bookmakers, and every change made to it with the test behind it.";
    var visitor = Visitor.Of(HttpContext);
    const string Repo = "https://github.com/TimDenby161/TheCornerFC";
    IHtmlContent Short(string iso) => Markup.LocalTime(DateTimeOffset.Parse(iso), "short", visitor);
}
<section class="panel mc" data-tab="model" data-active="true">
    @if (!Model.Ready)
    {
        <div class="empty-state" id="model-empty">The model's public record is being prepared. It is written by the nightly run.</div>
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="mc-env" id="model-updated">@if (Model.Version is not null){<text>Live model: @Model.Version · </text>}updated @Short(Model.Generated)</p>

        <h2 class="mc-h2">The record</h2>
        <p class="stats-note">Every figure comes from predictions stored before kick-off. The database refuses any change to a stored prediction, so this record can't be tidied up afterwards. Where the model trails the bookmakers, it says so.</p>
        <div class="stats-grid mc-tiles" id="model-tiles">
            @foreach (var t in Model.Tiles)
            {
                <div class="stats-card"><div class="stats-label">@t.Label</div><div class="stats-value mc-value"><span class="@t.Cls">@t.Value</span></div><div class="stats-note">@t.Note</div></div>
            }
        </div>
        <p class="stats-note">The model against the bookmakers on every bet market, competition by competition, is on the <a href="/stats">Stats</a> page.</p>

        @if (Model.Worked is { } ex)
        {
            <h2 class="mc-h2">One match, step by step</h2>
            <p class="stats-note">How the model made its prediction for @ex.Home v @ex.Away@(ex.Competition is { Length: > 0 } comp ? $" ({comp}, " : " (")@Short(ex.Kickoff)), from the inputs it had before kick-off to its chances. Every number is the one stored before the match. Final score: @ex.Home @ex.Hg–@ex.Ag @ex.Away. Any match's card shows the same breakdown under Model detail.</p>
            <div class="stats-card"><div class="why-detail mc-example" id="model-example">@await Html.PartialAsync("_DetailSections", (ex.Detail, true))</div></div>
        }

        <h2 class="mc-h2">Every change, and the test behind it</h2>
        <p class="stats-note">@Model.Registered changes are on the record. Each was written down, with how it would be judged, before its result was seen. Past figures are each change's own test on earlier matches; live figures are on matches played after it was written down.</p>
        @foreach (var (id, title, rows) in new[] { ("model-in", "In the model now", Model.InModel), ("model-tried", "Tried, or being tested", Model.Tried) })
        {
            if (rows.Count == 0) { continue; }
            <div class="stats-card"><div class="stats-label">@title</div>
                <div class="mc-scroll"><table class="calib-table mc-rows mc-versus" id="@id"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Change</th><th>Past matches</th><th>Past gain</th><th>Live matches</th><th>Live gain</th><th>On live matches</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>@foreach (var d in rows)
                    {
                        <tr class="mark-@d.Mark"><td class="mc-no">@ModelRecord.ShortId(d.Id)</td>
                            <td>@d.Title@if (d.ReadyNote != ""){<span class="mc-sub">@d.ReadyNote</span>}</td>
                            <td>@(d.N is { } n ? Js.Num(n) : "–")</td>
                            <td>@if (d.Gain is { } g){<span class="mc-gain mark-@d.Mark">@ModelRecord.Signed(g)</span>}else{<text>–</text>}</td>
                            <td>@(d.LiveRecord is { } lr ? Js.Num(lr.N) : "–")</td>
                            <td class="mc-live">@if (d.LiveRecord?.Gain is { } lg){@ModelRecord.Signed(lg)@if (d.LiveRecord.Low is { } lo && d.LiveRecord.High is { } hi){<span class="mc-sub">@ModelRecord.Signed(lo) to @ModelRecord.Signed(hi)</span>}}else{<text>–</text>}</td>
                            <td class="mc-live-say">@d.LiveText@if (d.LiveWhy != ""){<span class="mc-sub">@d.LiveWhy</span>}</td></tr>
                    }</tbody></table></div>
            </div>
        }
        <p class="stats-note">Gain is how much lower the log loss is with the change, so a plus is an improvement. Green: statistical evidence the change makes the model better. Red: evidence it makes it worse. No colour: not proven either way yet.
            @if (Model.LiveTests is { } lt){<text>Live tests: @Js.Num(lt.N) finished matches since @lt.Start, over @lt.Weeks week@(lt.Weeks == 1 ? "" : "s"), for @lt.Tracked change@(lt.Tracked == 1 ? "" : "s") (@lt.Protocol). Nothing is called before @lt.Matches matches and @lt.MinWeeks weeks, and the method allows looking at any time, which is why its ranges are wide.</text>}</p>

        <h2 class="mc-h2">Check it yourself</h2>
        <ul class="stats-note" id="model-check">
            <li>The model's code is public: <a href="@Repo/tree/main/thecornerfc/models" rel="noopener">the models</a>, and <a href="@Repo/tree/main/experiments/changes" rel="noopener">the register of every change</a>.</li>
            <li>Each model version is named by a fingerprint of its code files, so an edit, even a comment, makes a new version: <a href="@Repo/blob/main/tests/test_model_fingerprints.py" rel="noopener">the fingerprints</a>.</li>
            <li>Every test is written before its result is seen: <a href="@Repo/blob/main/experiments/prospective/PROTOCOLS.md" rel="noopener">the registered protocols</a>.</li>
            <li>What the measures mean and how each model works: <a href="/methodology">How the models work</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    }
</section>
